{
  "name": "Cover Letter",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "=Write a professional ATS-friendly cover letter for the position of {{ $json.positionTitle }} at {{ $json.companyName }}.\n\nCandidate Name:\n{{ $json.candidateName }}\n\nJob Description:\n{{ $json.jobDescription }}\n\nUsing the candidate's resume, write a personalized cover letter that:\n\n- Addresses the candidate by name.\n- Highlights relevant skills and experience.\n- Matches the job description.\n- Shows enthusiasm for the company and role.\n- Uses a professional and confident tone.\n- Is 200-280 words long.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nReturn ONLY the content that will go inside the cover letter.\n\nDo NOT return:\n- <!DOCTYPE html>\n- <html>\n- <head>\n- <body>\n- CSS\n- JavaScript\n- Markdown\n- Triple backticks\n- Explanations\n- Notes\n\nReturn only the cover letter text, starting with:\n\nDear Hiring Manager,\n\nand ending the cover letter MANDATORILY with the exact phrase:\n\nSincerely,\n{{ $json.candidateName }}\n"
            },
            {
              "id": "2",
              "name": "email",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.email }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "3",
              "name": "companyName",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.companyName }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "4",
              "name": "positionTitle",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.positionTitle }}"
            }
          ]
